From 894e4a8cd0b36e7d45532086ca60c0a6392b4926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Allen <callen.23dc@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:45:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the symbols Omperor and Upleft ask for, in their colours

Forty-two symbol names that Omperor's interface and Upleft's renderer
ask for had no drawing, so their images were nil: the crown before the
app's name and its turns, the sidebar's and Settings' row icons, the
Usage and model chips, the composer's paperclip, the Agents panel's
running and done marks, Thinking rows' sparkle, callout and code-block
glyphs. Each now has a line drawing on the 24-unit grid, in the style
of the others.

A configuration's colours were kept but never drawn: every symbol was
a black template, so a hierarchically coloured check in a text
attachment, which no view tints, came out black. A symbol with colours
of its own now draws in them and is not a template, as in AppKit. A
hierarchical colour inks a drawing's marks (what a plain one knocks out
of a filled shape) in the colour and the shape behind them at half its
strength; a palette gives the marks its first colour and the shape its
second.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
